INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (1, 2, 7, 4, 'It''s hard to objectively review this place. I''m biased toward liking it as I am Sri Lankan and prone to comparing everything made in this restaurant with home made fare. Overall, it''s a good taste of what Sri Lankan cuisine has to offer. From the lamprais with their banana leaf-wrapped selection of goodies to the hoppers, string hoppers and the range of vegetarian and meat curries, nothing fails to please the palate. There are even some real Sri Lankan soft drinks such as Necto available from time to time. My only gripe is the weird wording and kiwification of some of the meals. Lamprais (a Dutch word) are called Lump Rice (!), meat patties are flavoured differently and called curry puffs, and breadcrumb coated Chinese rolls are called curry rolls. I''m sure most modern Aucklanders could cope with the authentic terminology if given the chance. The only other downside of dining here is that there is no liquor license, so get your Necto on!', '2025-07-12 15:33:07.452423');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (2, 3, 7, 5, 'Great food but please Mr.Owner, I implore you, leave us to eat in peace! Enough with the stories of your life already, you''re a great chef, just please don''t hover around like an uncle who won''t leave Sunday dinner.', '2025-07-12 15:33:36.564106');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (3, 4, 7, 3, 'Food is not great but is ok . Seems one person show and cleanliness is mediocre. Not being a Srilankan can not rate taste ?', '2025-07-12 15:34:24.172937');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (4, 5, 7, 2, 'I wouldn''t rate this place for vegetarians. It was a long hungry wait (somewhere around 35-40 minutes) for the food. Maybe the guy serving was trying to do all the cooking too? I unwrapped the banana leaf and there was a ton of rice and three small blobs of curry. So basically vegetarians get half the amount of curry but pay the same! My husband and I both left hungry.', '2025-07-12 15:35:07.117372');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (5, 6, 7, 4, 'Sandringham is the place to head to when you fancy a curry. The spices and heady aromas mingle on the suburban streets to entice the punters in. And 7 Siri is no exception. One thing that does set this place apart though, is the origination of the curries. For 7 Siri serves Sri Lankan cuisine a more complex, light and spice-based style of eating in comparison to traditional Indian. The front window proudly displays large Dairy Free and Gluten Free signs, and you can eat a healthy, well-balanced meal here with a good mix of meat & vegetable curries. Delicious curry rolls, curry puffs & spicy skewers for starters; the legendary lump rice, masala dosa & a mouth-watering array of seafood curries such as prawn, crab or squid. Some of the more exotic dishes such as Appa, a crepe/roti hybrid formed into a crispy edible bowl to hold curries, eggs, or a delicious mix of vegetables & sliced roti are worth taking a chance on. There is even an icecream version!', '2025-07-12 15:39:04.888317');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (6, 7, 7, 5, 'Love this place! I was introduced to Sri Lankan food by a Sri Lankan ex in NYC. The relationship didn''t work out (thank god), but my love of Sri Lankan food remained!! It is somewhat like south indian cuisine, but has it''s own highlights. I was psyched to see that Auckland had a Sri Lankan spot in Sandringham, and I dream about the deliciousness between visits! Now that I''m a veggie, I don''t get the same stuff I used to, but thankfully the folks here can make just about any of their stuff vegetarian, and are quite happy to do so. I keep going back for the lump rice. The photo on the menu is deceiving as for some reason the photo makes it look like a tiny portion. Never fear, the portion is ample, and is plenty to stuff your face with. It comes out wrapped beautifully in a banana leaf, and inside is a selection of delicious curries, coconut, and rice. It is spicy and delicious! I also go for an appa with egg. It is a thin crepe like bowl with a runny egg cooked into the bottom of it. Just fabulous! The spot it small, but has a big table in the front that could fit about 8 people. It''s pretty casual and has takeaway, but feels cosy and homey. The owners, a husband and wife team seem to always be there, and are friendly and happy to make suggestions for the newbies! Check it out!', '2025-07-12 15:40:21.906363');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (7, 3, 480, 5, 'Amazing food. The lentil curry (Parippu) was my favourite. The staff were super friendly and our food was ready really quick. Great value for money, we got two large curries, one small curry, two rice and poppadom for only $24! No MSG or Preservatives!', '2025-07-12 16:17:18.253155');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (8, 9, 214, 5, 'Just great food. Small no frills place. Chili wontons are a must and the cucumber salad was a good refreshing balance. Grandma was making dumplings by hand right when you walk in like she does everyday. You prefer before you sit down so know what you want. Go here.', '2025-07-12 16:27:29.359566');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (9, 4, 214, 5, 'After a rather chilly day of city walking and very hungry, this was the perfect stop to warm up with hot and delicious noodle soup. I really love that they have clear yam noodles in addition to the traditional rice noodles. We ordered the beef brisket noodle soup, braised beef with tofu over rice, and dan-dan noodles. The taste is authentic, just the right amount of spicy hot and spicy ma2. Soup broth rich and tasting, not too oily. Good price, good value. Highly recommended.', '2025-07-12 16:28:04.789413');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (10, 10, 214, 5, 'The food was so good and warm. It was super chilly out when my trio sat down. The portions are large so come with an appetite! If you want some awesome authentic Chinese food, it''s worth the stop! I know when I go back to Auckland, I will be making a return stop!', '2025-07-12 16:28:42.817008');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (11, 7, 214, 5, 'Amazing little hole in the wall. Looks and tastes very authentic if you''re willing to not eat at some fancy looking place but rather want to eat somewhere the food is good. It''s spicy and they know it, keeping tissues on each table. You order up front. The food comes out pretty fast. One of the best places I ate while staying in Auckland.', '2025-07-12 16:29:48.329118');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (12, 5, 214, 1, 'Had Dan Dan Mian at Eden noodle commercial bay today. Worst Dan Dan Mian ever. It had Rocket lettuce which is a first! Hopefully last. Peanuts aren''t even chopped and all 7-8 of them is an extra. Yuk', '2025-07-12 16:30:22.841968');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (13, 10, 46, 2, 'Got pork done noodles. Pork had lots of pure Fat attached. Noodles ok. Very hot broth', '2025-07-12 16:34:22.37946');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (14, 7, 46, 4, 'Saw this on Yelp and it was in the hotel so when we had to go get food ASAP, I made it my mission to find Yong''s. It''s the bottom level of the Atrium on Elliott. Lots of options, but I ended up getting the egg and tomato noodle, which is my go to. Sauce was decent, and the noodles were pretty good. I also got some of the cold sides, which were my vegetable component, but they were super salty. Yikes. Overall, glad I found this spot. If you''re in the area, worth checking out.', '2025-07-12 16:35:11.310891');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (15, 11, 46, 4, 'Noodle crash: Miss the taste of #handpulled noodles and give the Yong''s a try. One dish was of #chicken flavor and the other #beef reminding us of Northeastern China. Yummy!', '2025-07-12 16:36:36.829784');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (17, 4, 46, 5, 'This was beyond expectation! So so good I ate here two nights in a row! It was affordable, easy, and just what I was looking for! Everything was fresh and the staff was very helpful with their menu. I wish I found this place sooner.', '2025-07-12 16:42:29.032528');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (34, 7, 558, 5, 'Amazing kitchen in the Park Hyatt Auckland. It''s not typical for us to eat in hotel restaurants, but this was the Park Hyatt after all! Plus, breakfast was included in our rate, and we saw such good reviews. Glad we didn''t miss it! Food was spectacular. Service was top notch. View was pretty. Highly recommended!', '2025-07-12 20:45:49.648888');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (16, 8, 46, 3, 'Hand pulled noodle is my favourite noodle dish. It originated in the Lan Zhou province of China. There used to be a small noodle house down in Christchurch year ago that made excellent renditions of it. So I was over joyed to find such a place in Auckland, right in the middle of CBD no less. The place was extra busy, I waited patiently for my noodle. This was the first time I had to actually yell at the waitress. Because they kept ignoring my bowl of noodle that was sitting on the pass. Once I got my steamy bowl of hand pulled strings. I realised that it resembled the famous Chinese offering somewhat. But after I have taken my first bite. I was hugely disappointed. The original hand pulled noodles are made with a solution containing the ashes from burning a certain grass. And the chemical within is called potassium carbonate. This is the chemical that gives the noodle dough it''s pliable character. What I got at yongs was close in texture to the original yet it felt like miles off also. I m not saying that yongs isn''t good for a cheap eat. It''s great if you just want a bowl of noodles. But if you are a hand pulled noodle aficionado, then you will be disappointed.', '2025-07-12 16:41:03.014966');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (18, 11, 220, 3, 'Food -four star. Restaurant ambiance - three star. Evil waitress - one star. Waitress was HELL BENT, telling us we ordered wrong when SHE clearly took our order down incorrectly. She went BALLISTIC and ranted at us for 10 minutes! Clearly INSANE. The other female waitress with the short, short shorts was so sweet and nice. The men liked looking at her butt cheeks every time she picked up and dropped off dishes to our table. Sweetie....your shorts need to be a tad more covering your ass', '2025-07-12 16:44:51.561295');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (22, 4, 556, 4, 'We came here because we wanted to try traditional Maori food and it was a really good first experience. Since we are new to this, I cannot speak to the authenticity of the food. Flavor and cooking wise, it was excellent. The lady suggested that we go with Lamb and Chicken Hangi since it was our first time. My friends took the chicken Hangi. Every Hangi is a plate of meat, cabbage, pumpkin, sweet potato (kumara) and boiled potato, with stuffing that resembles Indian khichdi or thanksgiving stuffing. Even though previous reviews had mentioned that the chicken was dry, I didn''t think the chicken was dry at all! Both the chicken and lamb were tender and easy to take off the bone. They were mildly spiced. The stuffing was delicious. I''m not a big fan of sweet potato but my friends thought it was the star of their plate. The pumpkin and the cabbage were delicious too. Everything came together as a full and filling meal. I''m glad that we got to experience this and I recommend coming here if you want to experience traditional Maori food. Just remember that you are coming for the food...the ambiance is not much to look at...just a no-nonsense restaurant. They cater. Lots of parking around the shop.', '2025-07-12 19:44:11.36446');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (23, 9, 556, 5, 'Really nice people running this place!! Food was very traditional and tasty!!! Loved visiting here, went back twice!', '2025-07-12 19:45:17.486545');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (24, 7, 556, 4, 'Traditional Moari style cooking. We got the chicken and lamb. Chicken with a little dry, with the lamb was so tender and fatty and delicious. The stuffing was delicious. The pumpkin and potato were a little bland. Good portions', '2025-07-12 19:45:52.32042');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (25, 3, 556, 5, 'I went to The Hangi Shop with my friend who had yet to try hangi. It tasted so good it brought tears to my eyes as flashes of my childhood came back to me. It was not at all bland and I felt the portions were generous', '2025-07-12 19:46:27.573164');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (26, 2, 556, 3, 'Sadly, there are very few options for getting Maori or Polynesian food in Auckland unless you''re at a family gathering, outdoor market or festival. I''m not a huge fan of the boil-up or hangi cause they tend to be on the bland and dry side, but the Hangishop Sammy packs in a lot of good flavor and texture. The sandwich comes with your choice of meat (pork, lamb or chicken), kamokamo pickle, red onions, kumara and watercress on toasted rewena bread. It definitely makes a visit to the Hangi Shop worthwhile. Kapai!', '2025-07-12 19:47:53.836453');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (27, 5, 557, 5, 'Absolutely delightful! I’ve dined here three times for the NZ Food Story set meal, and each visit brings a new, wonderfully surprising dish. The creativity and consistency are unmatched—this is, without question, the best tasting restaurant ever. I’ll definitely be coming back for more!', '2025-07-12 20:38:57.948914');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (28, 8, 557, 5, 'I enjoyed the vibrant atmosphere and the beautiful view of Auckland Harbour. The food was fresh and tasty, with ingredients sourced from all over New Zealand. We liked starters as well as mains although we didn’t try dessert menu. The drink menu is excellent, and the sommelier provided excellent advice on selecting the appropriate bottle.', '2025-07-12 20:39:53.802823');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (29, 3, 557, 5, 'You can’t fault this restaurant, it ticks all the boxes. The super friendly staff know every ingredient on the menu and take care and time to explain each item. The food is just delicious. Beautiful setting overlooking the ferry building and Harbour. Definitely an experience you must try.', '2025-07-12 20:40:36.002554');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (30, 10, 557, 5, 'The express lunch for 90$ pp is a value deal. The oyster is the best I’ve eaten so far. All dishes were full of complex, sometimes unusual flavors. We liked the chef’s creativity. Pretty view from the balcony and professional staff. Fantastic experience overall, we would definitely come back !', '2025-07-12 20:41:38.362666');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (31, 6, 557, 5, 'We had an amazing time at Ahi, the customer service provided by not only the servers but the chefs was amazing the food was definitely an experience I would recommend if you love to try new things, there were a couple new things I tried which took me by surprise but I’m not going to go into full detail about the food provided because that will take away from the amazing experience but to give you an idea I don’t like oysters but the oyster we tried was paired with a fresh flavour and it ended up being one of my favourite things that we ate. Highly highly recommend this for a unique experience!!', '2025-07-12 20:42:39.54554');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (32, 8, 558, 5, 'We got greeted by Kelly and Henry as host , she took our orders and we have great service from her team. Thanks to Ruby and Henry as the restaurant managers that made sure we got best table in the house. The food are delicious and really fresh. Really great experience to have lunch here. Few times came here, never been such disappointment. Very satisfying experience', '2025-07-12 20:43:29.143759');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (33, 3, 558, 5, 'This is in the Park Hyatt and you get exactly what you pay for - excellent. If you are after a nice dinner in Auckland, this is the place to experience it. Recommend their Oysters paired with Mignonette. Scotch Steak with the Black Peppercorn sauce. One of the best sauces I''ve had with any steak, compliments to the chefs for this recipe. Broccolini and Fries are great too. Excellent staff as well providing 5 star service. Thank you!', '2025-07-12 20:44:14.929577');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (20, 7, 220, 5, 'The restaurant has changed owners & it''s called Top Seafood Restaurant. We just got off cruise ship & wanted excellent Chinese food but not noodles or dumplings. Wow, what a find! The wonton soup is the best I ever had, better than most even in Hong Kong; filled with only fresh tender shrimp without any greasy meats. We ordered sizzling beef tenderloin. Prawns with garlic on rice noodles, & bochoy. The shrimp was butterflied & stuffed with garlic and it''s absolutely delicious. We were watching the table next to us & decided we want to come back the next night & try the other dishes. The water tank by the front door has severed varieties of fish, claims & lobsters. The service is excellent. They even made iced tea for my husband as we come to find out most NZ restaurants do not offer iced tea.', '2025-07-12 16:47:55.09164');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (21, 10, 220, 5, 'This restaurant is amazing. Food is delicious authentic Guangzhou food. Service is amazing. Altogether 5/5. DEFINITELY RECOMMEND', '2025-07-12 16:49:09.540755');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (35, 6, 558, 5, 'We had an exceptional dining experience at Onemate. The food was bursting with flavour, and the ambiance was absolutely stunning. The crayfish was cooked to perfection—juicy and delicious. Furthermore, the staff were friendly, attentive, and polite. Highly recommend this place for anyone visiting Auckland!', '2025-07-12 20:46:48.013226');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (36, 4, 558, 5, 'I would say I was impressed by the food:) We got a table by the window but it’s a bit shame that they said the next booking is around 1.5 hours later which made it a bit tight for us. Very nice food overall . The duck liver sauce was quite amazing. Fish crudo got a bit of fish sauce - tasted great. The venison was quite tender and well cooked. Loved the black pepper sauce served with the lamb rump. The mussle was very nice as well - interesting combination with potato slices with curry power :)', '2025-07-12 20:48:22.314272');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (37, 2, 480, 5, 'Dil Takeaways is an amazing place, to get delicious meals at an affordable price. However Im kindly letting you folks know that I arrived at your place at 12:18 today, as google said the restaurant opens at 1100. But the restaurant was closed. So please update your open amd closing times, or else it would have a negative impact on your place. Wish you all the best', '2025-07-12 20:50:32.454698');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (38, 7, 480, 4, 'A hidden gem, probably due to its location; a bit isolated. A small and nice place, value for money, great food in that range.. Had Egg roti and chicken curry during lunch for mere $14, worth it.. The menu is extensive and would love to try some other delicacies soon', '2025-07-12 20:51:45.607337');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (39, 11, 480, 4, 'If you want yummy Sri Lankan Rice and curry for a decent price look no further. I’ve tried many places around Auckland but hands down the best in terms of the value and quantity. 🤤👌🏽 Keep up the good work guys!', '2025-07-12 20:52:21.703709');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (40, 2, 561, 5, 'If you’re looking for authentic Sri Lankan flavours, warm hospitality and great value, THIS IS THE PLACE!!! The food here is absolutely delicious and George Niroshan (the manager on shift) was super friendly and welcoming. They also offer a 15% discount for students with ID, which makes it even better.', '2025-07-12 21:13:10.819933');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (41, 5, 561, 3, 'The food has been consistently great, and the prices are fair. However, I''ve noticed an issue with the wait times. On three separate occasions, I''ve had to wait 20 to 30 minutes longer than the time quoted when I placed my order', '2025-07-12 21:14:12.851136');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (42, 10, 561, 3, 'Lunch visit today group of 7, only one other table of 4 occupied. Food itself is pretty good - though the beef pepper fry was rather chewy/tough. However, service is decidedly NOT great. Took over 30 minutes for first dish to be served - when queried said kitchen busy as had Ubereats/takeaway orders to prepare. Unsure why online orders prioritised over dine-in guests. Salad did not turn up at all - when queried said would be another 5-10 minutes, so cancelled as would have been after we had finished. No napkins at the table or near the handwash station. Had to remind to get cutlery & plates when food finally arrived. Had to ask for water to be topped up. Had run out of all drinks except coke & sprite. No alcohol allowed due to ''public holiday'' - unsure why that is a reason either. All in all not a great experience. If you want the food, order takeaway as that apparently has priority & you are not sitting hungry waiting for your meal.', '2025-07-12 21:15:25.194073');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (43, 7, 561, 5, 'Enjoyed a fantastic family evening at the Grand Ceylon , The food was so delicious and beautifully presented, and the relaxed ambiance made it even better. Huge thanks to Jorge for his warm and professional service he truly went above and beyond. Definitely looking forward to our next visit!', '2025-07-12 21:16:17.57991');
INSERT INTO public.reviews VALUES (19, 5, 220, 4, 'We actually came this way meaning to try out some new Vietnamese place listed as hot and new, but could not find it so came here instead. It has changed since we had been by before, but never gone in, and was now open under new management, name and only just it''s 4th day. To celebrate the opening they had decorated the entry with floral arrangements which was a nice touch. Once in the restaurant , one will notice a quite sizable tank for lobster etc, a very clean and tidy interior, a few other ornaments like vases and the unusual one of a grandfather clock....I have never seen one of them before in a chinese restaurant. Something different .....a little strange but for me did not ruin the interior outlook at all. Service was good, with greeting on entering and quickly presented with menu at table. We ordered the Taiwanese soy sauce chicken ( 三杯鸡 ) and the Hong Kong style fried fish ( 避风塘炒鱼 ) . Soup of the day is bought to the table when you first sit down. That''s nothing flash, soup with veges and meat bone . Is common to give such soups to patrons in cantonese restaurants. Our food came out , was up to scratch...so much so that we nearly never had to takeaway the left overs. The price is a little high though. But still worth the expense. Chances we would come back', '2025-07-12 16:46:17.516762');